{"p":"/ui/text-input","t":"Text input fields","d":"Text input fields allow users to input text from their physical or on-screen keyboard.","h":"<p>import TextFiltering from '../includes/text-filtering/text-filtering.md'</p>\n<p>A <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/TextBox\"><code>TextBox</code></a> is a rectangle that allows a user to provide text input while it's in focus. When you <a href=\"#script-text-inputs\">script</a> a <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/TextBox\"><code>TextBox</code></a>, you can use it as a search bar or an input field on a form. To help users know what type of text they should input, you can also provide a prompt through the <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/TextBox/TextBox.PlaceholderText\"><code>PlaceholderText</code></a> property.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"data:image/webp;base64,\" /></p>\n<p>Because these objects are <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/GuiObject\"><code>GuiObjects</code></a>, you can customize\nproperties such as <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/GuiObject/GuiObject.BackgroundColor3\"><code>BackgroundColor3</code></a>,\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/GuiObject/GuiObject.BorderMode\"><code>BorderMode</code></a>,\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/GuiObject/GuiObject.Transparency\"><code>Transparency</code></a>, and\n<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/GuiObject/GuiObject.Rotation\"><code>Rotation</code></a> to fit the aesthetics of your game.</p>\n<h2>Create text inputs on the screen</h2>\n<p>A <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/TextBox\"><code>TextBox</code></a> on a screen is useful for\nthings like an input field for a form.</p>\n<p>To add a <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/TextBox\"><code>TextBox</code></a> to a screen:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>In the <strong>Explorer</strong> window, select <strong>StarterGui</strong> and add a <strong>ScreenGui</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Hover over StarterGui and click the &CirclePlus; button. A contextual menu displays.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Insert a <strong>ScreenGui</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Select the new <strong>ScreenGui</strong> and add a <strong>TextBox</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Hover over <strong>ScreenGui</strong> and click the &CirclePlus; button. A contextual menu displays.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Insert a <strong>TextBox</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Create text inputs on part faces</h2>\n<p>To add a <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/TextBox\"><code>TextBox</code></a> to the face of a part:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>In the <strong>Explorer</strong> window, select <strong>StarterGui</strong> and add a <strong>SurfaceGui</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Hover over StarterGui and click the &CirclePlus; button. A contextual menu displays.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Insert a <strong>ScreenGui</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Select the new <strong>SurfaceGui</strong> and add a <strong>TextBox</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Hover over <strong>SurfaceGui</strong> and click the &CirclePlus; button. A contextual menu displays.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Insert a <strong>TextBox</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Adorn the <strong>SurfaceGui</strong> to the <strong>part</strong> on which you want to display the <strong>TextBox</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>In the <strong>Properties</strong> window, select the <strong>Adornee</strong> property. Your cursor changes.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>In the <strong>Explorer</strong> window, select the part.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"callout c-warning\">\n<p>If you don't see the <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/TextBox\"><code>TextBox</code></a>, try <a href=\"#/docs/parts/textures-decals\">choosing a different face</a> in the <b>Face</b> property of the <b>SurfaceGui</b>.</p>\n</div>\n<h2>Script text inputs</h2>\n<p>Like <a href=\"#/docs/ui/buttons\">buttons</a>, you can script any action for a <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/TextBox\"><code>TextBox</code></a> object when a user interacts with it. For example, the following script connects the <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/TextBox/TextBox.FocusLost\"><code>FocusLost</code></a> event which fires when the user presses the <kbd>Enter</kbd> button or clicks outside the box. If <code>enterPressed</code> is <code>true</code>, meaning the user submitted the input instead of merely clicking outside the box, the script prints the contents of the entry to the <a href=\"https://create.roblox.com/docs/studio/output\">Output</a> window.</p>\n<p><strong>Basic Text Input Handling</strong></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-lua\">local textBox = script.Parent\n\nlocal function onFocusLost(enterPressed, inputObject)\n    if enterPressed then\n        print(textBox.Text)\n    end\nend\n\ntextBox.FocusLost:Connect(onFocusLost)\n</code></pre>\n<p>As another example, you might want to allow only numbers in a <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/TextBox\"><code>TextBox</code></a>. The following code uses the <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/TextBox/TextBox.GetPropertyChangedSignal\"><code>TextBox.GetPropertyChangedSignal</code></a> event to detect when the <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/TextBox/TextBox.Text\"><code>TextBox.Text</code></a> changes, such as when a user starts typing, then it uses the <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/library/string/string.gsub\"><code>string.gsub()</code></a> function to disallow non‑numbers.</p>\n<p><strong>Restricting Text Input to Numbers</strong></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-lua\">local textBox = script.Parent\n\nlocal function allowOnlyNumbers()\n    textBox.Text = string.gsub(textBox.Text, &quot;%D&quot;, &quot;&quot;)\nend\n\ntextBox:GetPropertyChangedSignal(&quot;Text&quot;):Connect(allowOnlyNumbers)\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Text filtering</h2>","kid":{"simple":"A `TextBox` is a box where players can type, like a search bar, a name field, or a code entry pad. You can show it on the screen or on a part. Scripts can notice when the player finishes typing and then use what they wrote. Because players can type anything, you must filter their text before other people see it.","analogy":"A `TextBox` is like a blank line on a form. The `PlaceholderText` is the light gray hint that says what to write, and it disappears when you start typing.","keyPoints":["A `TextBox` lets a player type when it is in focus (selected).","`PlaceholderText` shows a hint, like \"Enter your name\", before the player types.","To add one to the screen: put a `ScreenGui` in `StarterGui`, then a `TextBox` in it.","To add one to a part: put a `SurfaceGui` in `StarterGui`, add the `TextBox`, then set the `SurfaceGui`'s `Adornee` to the part.","The `FocusLost` event fires when the player presses Enter or clicks away; its first value tells you if Enter was pressed.","`GetPropertyChangedSignal(\"Text\")` lets you react every time the text changes, for example to allow only numbers.","You are responsible for filtering any text players type before showing it to others, or Roblox may remove your game."],"terms":{"focus":"When a text box is selected and ready for typing. Clicking the box gives it focus; pressing Enter or clicking away removes it.","FocusLost":"An event that fires when the box stops being selected.","enterPressed":"True if the player pressed Enter to finish, false if they just clicked somewhere else.","PlaceholderText":"Gray hint text shown when the box is empty.","GetPropertyChangedSignal":"Gives you an event that fires when one specific property changes, like `Text`.","string.gsub":"A function that finds and replaces parts of text. With the pattern `%D` it finds every character that is not a digit.","text filtering":"Roblox's system that hides bad words and personal info, like phone numbers, from text."},"example":{"title":"Read what the player typed when they press Enter","place":"LocalScript inside a TextBox (inside a ScreenGui in StarterGui)","code":"local textBox = script.Parent\ntextBox.PlaceholderText = \"Type a number and press Enter\"\n\n-- Only allow digits: remove anything that is not 0-9\nlocal function allowOnlyNumbers()\n\tlocal cleaned = string.gsub(textBox.Text, \"%D\", \"\")\n\tif cleaned ~= textBox.Text then\n\t\ttextBox.Text = cleaned\n\tend\nend\n\nlocal function onFocusLost(enterPressed)\n\tif enterPressed then\n\t\tprint(\"You typed:\", textBox.Text)\n\tend\nend\n\ntextBox:GetPropertyChangedSignal(\"Text\"):Connect(allowOnlyNumbers)\ntextBox.FocusLost:Connect(onFocusLost)","explain":["We set a hint in `PlaceholderText`.","Every time the text changes, we remove any character that is not a digit using `string.gsub` and `%D`.","We only set `Text` again if something was removed, so we do not cause extra change events.","When the box loses focus, we check `enterPressed`; if the player pressed Enter, we print what they typed."]},"watchOut":["Never show one player's typed text to other players without running it through Roblox's text filtering first.","`FocusLost` also fires when the player clicks away. Check `enterPressed` if you only want real submissions.","Text a player types in a `LocalScript` stays on their device. To use it on the server, you need to send it with a `RemoteEvent`."]}}